 3.5 Mutual Exclusion — Hardware Approaches
Hardware provides atomic instructions that test-and-modify or swap memory words without interruption: test-and-set and
compare-and-swap (also atomic variables and memory barriers).

Test-and-Set

 boolean test_and_set(boolean *target) { /* executed atomically */
 boolean rv = *target; /* remember the old value */
 *target = true; /* always set the lock */
 return rv; /* return the ORIGINAL value */
